      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1883 Confederate veterans chose Brighton as the permanent site for their annual reunion, a gathering that peaked at 15,000 in 1897.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brighton%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Brighton became an incorporated town in 1913 under a Tennessee charter that still governs it today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brighton%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town prides itself on low property taxes, top‑rated schools, and welcoming churches that keep neighbors close.",
